Summary: Wait up to 120 s, not 10 s, for explorer to set up the desktop
Category: system
Kind: fix
Origin: wine-mac-builds
  Note: dlls/win32u/winstation.c (get_desktop_window); written for
    wine-mac-builds.
Upstream: no (candidate; draft in .local/bug-reports/)
Why: The first process of a session to need the desktop starts
 explorer.exe /desktop and waits for it to go idle, which it does once it
 has loaded the display driver, created the desktop window and registered
 the display devices. The wait gave up after 10 s. The process then had the
 server create a bare desktop window, which has no display-device GUID, so
 load_desktop_driver found no GraphicsDriver and the process stayed on the
 null driver for the rest of its life ("The explorer process failed to
 start.", nodrv_CreateWindow): no windows, no Direct3D device. With every
 core busy under Rosetta, explorer can take far longer than 10 s. The wait
 is now 120 s; it still ends at once if explorer exits.
Programs: Second Chance (an app that embeds Wine), with nine games
 starting at once on one Mac: Secrets Can Kill Remastered crashed on a null
 Direct3D object 10 s in, installers and patchers exited non-zero, an AutoIt
 script exited without a window. Second Chance now starts explorer itself
 and waits for its display devices first.
Uncertain: Explorer took about 2.5 minutes there under the heaviest load,
 longer than this wait too; a host should still start explorer first, as
 Second Chance does. The wait is in the program's first window or GDI call,
 so a program whose explorer never goes idle now stalls up to 120 s
 instead of 10 s before getting the null driver.
Evidence: With explorer made 15 s late before it creates the desktop (a
 graphics driver listed before the Mac driver that sleeps 15 s in DllMain
 and then fails), a program's CreateWindowEx failed after 10.1 s on 11.22
 (host11 tree, macOS 26.7.2); with this change it got its window after 17
 to 18 s. Holding explorer back before Wine starts in it doesn't show the
 bug: NtCreateUserProcess waits for the child to start, with no timeout.
Status: 2026-11-22 (later): in host14 (build0 + 0068-0074), Second Chance's full
 hosted integration run on meeka passed every source: disc 36/36, download
 6/6, Her downloads 3/3, Steam 11/11, Big Fish owned and trial. Secrets
 Can Kill Remastered's trial needed reruns (its DRM ended without starting
 the game, no Wine errors), as on host8 and host10 before these patches.
 2026-11-22: not yet in a build. Tested by swapping a win32u.so
 built with it into the host11 tree on meeka (macOS 26.7.2): the
 regression test desktop-wait passes (2 runs); on host11 it fails (1 run).
 The full suite on that tree: 54 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped (the
 screen-taking tests, WMB_REGRESS_NO_SCREEN).

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/winstation.c b/dlls/win32u/winstation.c
--- a/dlls/win32u/winstation.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/winstation.c
@@ -894,7 +894,11 @@
         {
             NtResumeThread( thread, NULL );
             TRACE_(win)( "started explorer\n" );
-            NtUserWaitForInputIdle( process, 10000, FALSE );
+            /* Explorer sets up the desktop and its display devices before it goes idle;
+             * without them this process gets the null driver for good. With every core
+             * busy that can take much longer than 10 s. The wait also ends if explorer
+             * exits. */
+            NtUserWaitForInputIdle( process, 120000, FALSE );
             NtClose( thread );
             NtClose( process );
         }
